<h2>Beyond our published range</h2>
<p>The product pages on this site cover what we export most consistently. They aren't the limit of what we can source.</p>

<p>We're a full-fledged export house rather than a single-commodity trader, and a meaningful share of our business comes from buyers asking for something adjacent to our published range — a related grade, a processed form of something we already handle, or a product our sourcing network can reach even though it isn't on the site.</p>

<h2>What we need from you</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>The product and specification</strong> — as precisely as you can state it.</li>
  <li><strong>Quantity</strong> — per shipment, and whether this is one-off or recurring.</li>
  <li><strong>Destination port.</strong></li>
  <li><strong>Any compliance requirements</strong> your market imposes — documentation, testing, certification.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What you'll get back</h2>
<p>A straight answer. If we can source it at the grade and volume you need, we'll quote. If we can source it but only in different grades or volumes, we'll say that. If we can't, or if it's currently export-restricted from India, we'll tell you and explain why rather than stringing out a conversation that isn't going anywhere.</p>

<h2>A note on export restrictions</h2>
<p>India's export policy on agricultural commodities changes more often than most buyers expect. Products have moved between free, restricted and prohibited status with limited notice in recent years. Before we quote any product, we confirm its current position with DGFT rather than assuming. If you're planning a programme around a specific Indian-origin commodity, that's worth factoring into your risk planning — and worth asking us about early.</p>

<h2>Start the conversation</h2>
<p>Send your requirement through the form below or via WhatsApp. If it's something we handle regularly, you'll usually have a quote within 24 business hours. If it's something we need to check sourcing on, we'll tell you how long that will take rather than leaving you waiting.</p>
